WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.640
I think one of the worst things that

00:00:01.439 --> 00:00:06.480
people can do is go from, you know, in

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.000
my book, I I had a framework of three

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.679
things you need to operate at a high

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.559
level. You need business, you need cash,

00:00:11.679 --> 00:00:13.599
because [clears throat] people don't

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:15.599
realize it's really hard to run a

00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:17.279
company without money. You got no cash

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:20.160
coming in. You got no cash in your bank.

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:21.680
Very, very hard to run and grow company.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.000
The second thing you need is a network,

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.840
people to hire and people to, you know,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.840
buy from you. The third thing you need

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.760
is operational chops. You need skills.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.079
You need ability. At the beginning, you

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.600
have none of that. So, is that the best

00:00:32.079 --> 00:00:36.160
time to go buy company and take a risk

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.840
on that? No. In my opinion, that first

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.320
business is about acquiring those three

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.480
things. Trade your time for money,

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.760
exercise the muscles, acquire those

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.280
three things. Learn how to operate a

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.120
company, accumulate a little bit of

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:49.120
capital, get that network, find some

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.239
people who know you and people who you

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.760
know, you know, and then go on to a

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:55.760
better business if if you find a better

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.199
opportunity. So, for me, it was, hey, I

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.320
didn't have any operational chops. I

00:00:57.199 --> 00:01:00.640
didn't have the ability to raise any

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.920
capital. I didn't have um a bunch of,

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:06.320
you know, a massive network. So, I

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:08.240
traded my time for money and ran around

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:09.920
in a sweaty startup and acquired those

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.360
three things. Then I got into a better

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.799
business which was self- storage. First

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:14.240
one was a moving and storage company. We

00:01:12.799 --> 00:01:16.560
did pick up a delivery box. It's a

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:18.159
brutal, brutal business. Then we went

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.759
into self storage and raised a bunch of

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:21.680
capital for that which is a much much

00:01:19.759 --> 00:01:23.119
better business. And now I've went on to

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:25.360
acquire some ownership stakes and start

00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:26.479
some other businesses as well. But man,

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.680
that stuff would be really hard if I had

00:01:26.479 --> 00:01:30.640
to try to skip some of those early

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:32.799
steps. So, so, so I feel pretty strongly

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:35.600
that your first business is not

00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:37.680
necessarily the last business and it's

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:38.720
not necessarily,

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.280
you know, the business that's going to

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.880
make all of your dreams come true. It's

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.360
it's really kind of about acquiring

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:48.560
these skills and and you know, mindsets

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:50.399
that I talk about in this startup book.

